# A contract's battle on the port with the 1990 BTECH: walk, turn, fire,
# the HUD keys, pause and the retreat dialog, a jump, the inspection and
# order screens, then the battle ends on its own and the campaign resumes.
# random: the words the original's copy protection left (its screen's), so
# the campaign starts as it did with it and this battle ends on its own.
random:178ab0ad
Return Return Down Down Return Return Left Return @snap:accepted Return @snap:deploy
Return
ticks:0 @snap:briefing               # the lance map, waiting for a key
Return ticks:10 @snap:cockpit
make:Up ticks:40 break:Up ticks:20 @snap:walking
make:Left ticks:15 break:Left ticks:1 @snap:turned
Space ticks:1 @snap:fired
2 ticks:1 Space ticks:1 @snap:fired2
Tab ticks:40 @snap:cycle
Tab ticks:1 W ticks:1 @snap:group
W ticks:1 T ticks:1 R ticks:1 Z ticks:1 @snap:hud       # T: heading radar; empty slots read a null torso
Z ticks:1 Z ticks:1 T ticks:1 Return ticks:1 @snap:target
P ticks:5 @snap:paused
Space ticks:5 @snap:unpaused
Escape ticks:5 @snap:retreat_ask
N ticks:5 @snap:retreat_no
J ticks:20 @snap:jump
ticks:60 @snap:landed                # a hard landing: the mech falls
D ticks:5 @snap:inspection
Space ticks:5 @snap:inspection_back
C ticks:5 @snap:orders               # no lancemates: the empty panel's null control
Down ticks:2 Return ticks:2 @snap:orders_command
Space ticks:5 @snap:orders_back
idle:0 @snap:results                 # the battle is decided and ends by itself; the campaign
Return @snap:after
